<title>USA: UN okays deeper discount for Iraq oil sales to U.S. [CORRECTED 18:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>UN okays deeper discount for Iraq oil sales to U.S. [CORRECTED 18:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Nations sanctions committee on Iraq has approved deeper discounts for Iraqi crude sales to the U.S., diplomatic sources said Thursday.</p>
<p>The committee met requests by Iraq's State Oil Marketing Organisation (SOMO) to deepen discounts to account for deteriorating sour crude prices in the U.S., the sources said.</p>
<p>The price for U.S.-bound Basrah Light crude will drop to $3.90 a barrel below benchmark West Texas Intermediate from March 10. The committee also allowed a special discount price of $4.30 below WTI for February and up to March 9, down from the originally agreed $3.85 under. (Corrects name of crude referred to from Kirkuk Blend, to Basrah Light).</p>
</text>
